TiVo's kernel has a sync right after the sc of clear_bit() (all 374 device sites: "ll; and; sc; sync"
inside the retry loop), and nowhere else in the bitops/atomics: set_bit, change_bit, test_and_*,
atomics and spinlocks match stock 3.3. No Broadcom stblinux-3.3 release (2.5 .. 4.4) or 3.14 has it,
so it is a TiVo change (likely a BMIPS5000 ll/sc workaround). Only the ll/sc path used on BMIPS5000
(non-R10000, non-MIPSR2) is patched.

--- a/arch/mips/include/asm/bitops.h
+++ b/arch/mips/include/asm/bitops.h
@@ -158,6 +158,7 @@ static inline void clear_bit(unsigned long nr, volatile unsigned long *addr)
 			"	" __LL "%0, %1		# clear_bit	\n"
 			"	and	%0, %2				\n"
 			"	" __SC "%0, %1				\n"
+			"	sync					\n"
 			"	.set	mips0				\n"
 			: "=&r" (temp), "+m" (*m)
 			: "ir" (~(1UL << bit)));
